{
  "slug": "expressions-and-simplifying",
  "name": "Expressions & simplifying",
  "strand": "Algebra",
  "dfeUnit": "Expressions and equations: notation & simplifying (Y7)",
  "description": "Algebraic notation, collecting like terms and substitution.",
  "yearGroup": 7,
  "planned": 15,
  "questions": [
    {
      "key": "alg-five-more-than-n",
      "band": 1,
      "archetype": "G",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "A pen costs n pence. A pencil costs 5p more than a pen. Which expression gives the cost of a pencil?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "n + 5",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "5n",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-WRITE-EXPRESSION"
        },
        {
          "text": "n − 5",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-WRITE-EXPRESSION"
        },
        {
          "text": "5 − n",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-WRITE-EXPRESSION"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "\"5 more than n\" means add 5: n + 5. Writing 5n means 5 times n. \"More than\" is not a multiplication word, so it is not 5n, and it is not a subtraction either."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-divided-by-2",
      "band": 2,
      "archetype": "G",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Which expression means \"a divided by 2\"?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "a/2",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "2/a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-NOTATION-DIV"
        },
        {
          "text": "a − 2",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-OP-CONFUSE"
        },
        {
          "text": "2a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-OP-CONFUSE"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Dividing a by 2 is written a/2: the number being divided goes on top. Writing 2/a divides 2 by a, which is the other way round, and 2a multiplies instead of dividing."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-3a-as-sum",
      "band": 2,
      "archetype": "C",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Which expression is equal to 3a?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "a + a + a",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "a × a × a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-TERM-COUNT"
        },
        {
          "text": "3 + a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-ADD-COEFFICIENT"
        },
        {
          "text": "a + 3",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-ADD-COEFFICIENT"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "3a means three lots of a, which is a + a + a. a × a × a is a³, not 3a. 3 + a and a + 3 mean 3 added to a, which is different: if a is 4, 3a is 12 but 3 + a is 7."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-simplify-5x-3y",
      "band": 1,
      "archetype": "E",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Simplify 5x + 3y.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "5x + 3y",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "8xy",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-UNLIKE-TERMS"
        },
        {
          "text": "8x + y",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-UNLIKE-TERMS"
        },
        {
          "text": "15xy",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-UNLIKE-TERMS"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "5x and 3y are not like terms: one is a number of x's and the other a number of y's, so they cannot be combined. The expression is already as simple as it gets. Adding the coefficients gives 8xy, which treats them as like terms."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-multiply-2a-3a",
      "band": 4,
      "archetype": "C",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Simplify 2a × 3a.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "6a²",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "6a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-MULT-NOT-ADD"
        },
        {
          "text": "5a²",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-MULT-NOT-ADD"
        },
        {
          "text": "5a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-UNLIKE-TERMS"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "2a × 3a = 2 × a × 3 × a = 6 × a × a = 6a². Multiplying the coefficients (2 × 3 = 6) and the letters (a × a = a²) keeps them separate. Writing 6a adds the letters instead of multiplying, and 5a² adds the coefficients instead of multiplying."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-error-collecting",
      "band": 3,
      "archetype": "D",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Jaz writes 2a + 3b = 5ab. What has she done?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Collected terms that are not like terms",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Multiplied the terms instead of adding them",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-MULT-NOT-ADD"
        },
        {
          "text": "Added the coefficients but not the letters",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-ADD-COEFFICIENT"
        },
        {
          "text": "Left the expression with two terms",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-UNLIKE-TERMS"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "2a and 3b are unlike terms, so 2a + 3b cannot be simplified. Jaz has combined the 2 and the 3 and joined the letters to get 5ab. If a and b were both 1, the expression would be 5 but 5ab would be 5 too — the error only shows with other values."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-substitute-3a",
      "band": 3,
      "archetype": "A",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Work out the value of 3a when a = −2.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "−6",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "6",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-SUBSTITUTE-NEG"
        },
        {
          "text": "−1",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-OP-CONFUSE"
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-OP-CONFUSE"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "3a means 3 × a, so 3 × (−2) = −6. The negative sign applies to the whole value, so the answer is negative. Adding instead of multiplying gives 3 + (−2) = 1, and 3 − 2 = 1 too."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-substitute-square",
      "band": 3,
      "archetype": "A",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Work out the value of a² when a = −3.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "9",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "−9",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-SUBSTITUTE-NEG"
        },
        {
          "text": "−6",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-A-SQUARED-2A"
        },
        {
          "text": "6",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-A-SQUARED-2A"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "a² means a × a, so (−3) × (−3) = 9. A negative times a negative is positive, so it is not −9. Multiplying by 2 instead of squaring gives −6."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-simplify-a-plus-a-squared",
      "band": 4,
      "archetype": "C",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Simplify a + a².",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "a + a²",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "2a²",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-LIKE-TERMS-POWER"
        },
        {
          "text": "2a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-LIKE-TERMS-POWER"
        },
        {
          "text": "a³",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-LIKE-TERMS-POWER"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "a and a² are not like terms: one is a and the other is a × a. They cannot be collected, so the expression stays as a + a². Adding to get 2a² or 2a, or multiplying to get a³, all treat them as like terms."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-bridge-perimeter",
      "band": 3,
      "archetype": "G",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "bridge": true,
      "prompt": "A rectangle is a cm long and 3 cm wide. Which expression gives its perimeter in cm?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "2a + 6",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "a + 3",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-WRITE-EXPRESSION"
        },
        {
          "text": "3a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-WRITE-EXPRESSION"
        },
        {
          "text": "2a + 3",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-WRITE-EXPRESSION"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The perimeter is a + 3 + a + 3 = 2a + 6. a + 3 adds only one length and one width, and 3a multiplies instead of adding. 2a + 3 doubles the length but forgets to double the width."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-tick-equal-5a",
      "band": 2,
      "archetype": "B",
      "answerType": "MULTI_SELECT",
      "prompt": "Choose every expression equal to 5a.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "a + a + a + a + a",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "5 × a",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "2a + 3a",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "5 + a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-ADD-COEFFICIENT"
        },
        {
          "text": "a × a × a × a × a",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "ALG-TERM-COUNT"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "5a means five lots of a: a + a + a + a + a, which is also 5 × a, and 2a + 3a collects to 5a. 5 + a adds 5 to a, which is different, and a × a × a × a × a is a⁵."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-not-equal-3a-plus-2a",
      "band": 2,
      "archetype": "E",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Which expression is not equal to 3a + 2a?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "6a",
          "correct": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "5a",
          "correct": 0,
          "catches": "ALG-MULT-NOT-ADD"
        },
        {
          "text": "a + a + a + a + a",
          "correct": 0,
          "catches": "ALG-MULT-NOT-ADD"
        },
        {
          "text": "5 + a",
          "correct": 0,
          "catches": "ALG-ADD-COEFFICIENT"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "3a + 2a is 3 lots of a plus 2 lots of a, which is 5 lots of a: 5a, or a + a + a + a + a. 6a comes from multiplying the coefficients instead of adding them. 5 + a adds 5 to a, which is different."
    },
    {
      "key": "alg-retention-not-equal-4x",
      "band": 1,
      "archetype": "E",
